<ContentPage
	title="About JPG to PDF Online"
	description="Learn about JPG to PDF Online, a simple browser-based converter for preparing JPG images as PDFs with a chosen file-size target."
	eyebrow="About this tool"
>
	<p>JPG to PDF Online is a focused utility for turning JPG and JPEG images into a PDF. Add one image or a group, arrange the pages, and choose the document settings that suit your task.</p>
	<section aria-labelledby="about-purpose"><h2 id="about-purpose" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Why we made it</h2><p class="mt-2">Some online forms set a maximum attachment size. Photos can produce a PDF that is too large to submit, so this converter lets you choose a maximum target and checks the actual PDF it creates. Smaller targets can reduce image dimensions or quality, and not every set of images can meet every limit.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="about-privacy"><h2 id="about-privacy" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">A browser-based approach</h2><p class="mt-2">Image conversion happens in your browser. The selected images are not sent to a conversion server, and you do not need an account. The website itself is still served over the web, where routine connection data may be handled by the hosting infrastructure.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="about-users"><h2 id="about-users" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Who it is for</h2><p class="mt-2">It is designed for anyone who needs to combine JPG or JPEG images into a straightforward PDF, including people preparing documents for application forms or other upload portals.</p></section>
</ContentPage>
